The monster sound MS_SHRIEK (commonly issued by Shrieker Mushrooms)
has something like 1 chance in 200 of summoning a Purple Worm to that
level.  Moral of the story: don't let them shriek.

Just a couple days ago, I saw a Purple Worm on Dungeon Level 1.
I was playing a Wizard at the time, and new that I could get a
lot of mileage my scratching with my athame.  However, since I
was still level 4 at the time, I decided to leave the level,
and come back when I could get the Full XP value of the worm.
(Otherwise, I'd only be given enough XP to be 1 short of level 6).

A little later, my not-so-butch Level 6 wizard (Str 10 or so, armed with
a +0 curved sword) decided to go back and take on the Level 15
Purple Worm.  (who says spell-casters are wimps?)

I engraved as soon as I got there, ditched a couple sewer rats
which were in my way, and proceeded to swing at the worm, keeping
my eye on the ground.  (Didn't want to scuff up my calligraphy.)
Each time the worm came close I swung at it.  This lasted for a while.

Unfortunately, the purple worm was getting hungrier and angrier,
and he finally noticed a scuff mark before I did, and immediately
took the initiative to swallow me.  Well, that was my signal to
use the big guns: all 3 zaps of the lightning wand I started with.
And that was enough!  (as my XP more than doubles)

The amusing thing about this wizard is that aside from a ring of warning,
this is the first time he had used any of his magic items.  I did all
the rest with pure fighter-oid hack and slay.  I even got to level 9
without casting any spells, or using any known scrolls other than identify.
I even still had my 'enchant weapon' and 'gain level' from my starting
equipment.

Unfortunately a game crash nuked my character (sob sob).  No save file
in the save directory;  no record in the score list or the logfile.
Not a trace!  I'm incredibly bummed about that.

